<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33722" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλιξ</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐκος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, as
		Adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>twisted,
				curved</i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, as in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				374
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.127
			</span></i>, epith. of oxen, commonly understood of their <i>twisted,
				crumpled horns</i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλικτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			; also expld. of the movement of their bodies as they walk,
				<i>rolling</i>: freq. coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰλίπους</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.293
			</span></i> and Sch. ad loc., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλιξ</span> abs.,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1170
			</span></i> (lyr.): later of various objects, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				221 ix 15
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕλικα ἀνὰ χλόαν</span> on the
				<i>tangled</i> grass, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				180
			</span></i> (lyr., cf. sq. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρόμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					2.263
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σειρή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					322
				</span></i>
			.</div>
